{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And as for Ishmael, I have heard you, etc.</b> That is: and as for Ishmael — I will bless him on account of the prayer that you pray over him, but not on account of the covenant that belongs to Isaac." "<b>Twelve.</b> He will beget twelve princes. Ishmael had twelve sons, and they are specified by name at the end of the parashah of ויהיו חיי שרה, where it is written there: the firstborn of Ishmael, Nebaioth, and Kedar, and Adbeel, and Mibsam, and Mishma, and Dumah, and Massa, Hadad, and Tema, Jetur, Naphish, and Kedemah — behold, twelve. And the reason it said 'twelve princes' (נשיאים) and did not say 'twelve nations (גוים) he will beget' is to indicate their exaltation and their great eminence, that the blessing of multiplicity would rest upon them more than upon other peoples, as the Holy One, blessed be He, promised him: 'Behold, I have blessed him, and I will make him fruitful, and I will multiply him very greatly.' Furthermore, the word נשיאים also includes the meaning that they will perish from the world after the great eminence — for it is from the language of (Proverbs 25:14) 'נשיאים ורוח,' and this comes to hint that they are consumed and lost from the world, in the language of (Job 7:9) 'כלה ענן וילך.' This is why you find נשיאם written deficient in its final yod (יו״ד), and Scripture thereby teaches you about the kingdom of Ishmael: its beginning is strong and its end fades — and likewise the angel said to Hagar: 'and he shall be a wild ass of a man,' that is, that he will be among the children of men like a wild ass that overpowers everything, and afterward 'his hand shall be against all.'" "<b>And I will make him a great nation.</b> Rabbenu Hananel, of blessed memory, wrote: we have seen that this promise was delayed for them two thousand three hundred and thirty-three years, and their delay was not contingent upon their sin; they were waiting for it all those years, and in the end it came and was fulfilled, and afterward the kingdom was strengthened in their hand. We, from whom it was taken because of our sins — and the set time for it is one thousand three hundred and thirty years — how much more so must we be expecting His promise and not despair. Thus far."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:59.563437261Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}